course: dictionary
lesson: 11503
title: Agreeably: pleasant and willing
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Agreeably» is an adverb. It tells you how something is done, or how someone feels about it. It comes from the word «agreeable», which means pleasant or nice.
explain: «The old man agreeably helped us carry the heavy bags.» Did he help us grumpily or kindly? The sentence shows he was willing and friendly, so agreeably means in a pleasant, willing way.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The old man in a pleasant, willing way helped us carry the heavy bags.» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: «Agreeably» means in a pleasant, nice way, or in a friendly, willing way.
fact: «Agreeably» is an adverb, so it describes how something happens or how someone does something.
fact: «Agreeably surprised» means pleasantly surprised: something nice happened when you did not expect it.
fact: «Agreeable» is the adjective, and «agreeably» is the adverb made from it.
exercise: «The villagers agreeably shared their bread with the travellers.» How did the villagers share? | Very slowly, one crumb at a time | In secret, when nobody was looking | *In a friendly, willing way | Rudely, with a grumble
exercise: Dad says, «I was agreeably surprised by the price of the tickets.» What does agreeably surprised mean? | Surprised by a loud noise | *Pleasantly surprised | Bored and sleepy | Shocked and angry
exercise: «The room was agreeably warm, so we took off our coats.» What does agreeably mean here? | *In a nice, pleasant way | Very loudly | Cold and damp | Too hot to touch
test:
«The children agreeably tidied their rooms when they were asked.» What does agreeably mean here? | Angrily | *Willingly and pleasantly | Quietly, under the bed | Sadly
«The shopkeeper smiled and agreeably gave us a free sweet.» What does agreeably suggest? | Unkindly, to make us go away | Reluctantly, with a frown | *Kindly and willingly | By accident
exam:
Ella's friend says, «The new teacher spoke agreeably to everyone.» What does agreeably tell you about the teacher? | Loud and cross | Asleep at her desk | *Pleasant and friendly | Very tall
